  "premise": "Silas Ashgrove, concierge of the Marlowe Grand Hotel, has spent fifteen years quietly recording the town of Port Ellery's secrets in a private ledger. When twin letters arrive at the front desk—one a murder confession, one promising a second killing at the tide's turning—Silas realizes the writer knows about the ledger and is using it as a stage. Partnering with disgraced former detective Maren Kettle, Silas discovers the confession points to a drowning fifteen years ago that the town's most powerful family buried. The killer is the victim's sibling, now the hotel's owner, who has been feeding Silas secrets for years to build an unimpeachable witness. In the tide caves below the cliffs, Silas traps the killer into a second confession, choosing justice outside the law by publishing the ledger rather than letting the family buy silence, and the tide finally gives up what it took.",
  "about_author": "Coral Whitlock spent a decade working night desks at coastal hotels before turning to crime fiction, collecting the overheard confessions of travelers who mistook anonymity for safety. She writes from a rented room above a lighthouse keeper's cottage, where the tide dictates her working hours.",
